  "lookup_name": "Trans_Pre",
  "description": "The cube, then its differences, and the room climbs to show them. One yellow block stands alone behind a two-metre wall. Round it and east, the same block stands four cells on and a metre up, and you take the ramp to reach it: that is translation, and the ramp is the part of the vector you can walk. On the shelf above, a copy turned forty-five degrees and a copy one and a half times the size. On the summit, a copy moved, turned and grown at once, which is what one matrix does. Then a wall with one door, and beyond it the same three in time: a cube that only rises and falls, a cube that only turns, a cube that only grows and shrinks, and one doing all three at once. Beside it stands a plain pick-up cube, which does the first two and has all along - the third it performs once, as you take it.",
