 "documentation": {
  "summary": "Trans_Pre - the cube transformation primer: three differences in space, then the same three in time",
  "layout": "An 11x27 hall. Three levels joined by wedges hold the five static stages; a threshold wall with one door closes them off, and the motion gallery is the flat hall beyond it.",
  "objective": "See each transformation as the difference between a cube and its copy, then as the same difference applied over and over, and find that the pick-up cube's own idle animation is two of the three.",
  "key_elements": [ "mario_cube alone at (5,3), behind the inner wall across row 4", "the pair at row 5: translation, four cells east and a metre up the wp:90 at (7,5)", "the pair at row 9 on the shelf: rotation (mario_cube:45:0)", "the pair at row 12, same two columns: scale (mario_cube:0:0:1.5)", "the pair at row 16 on the summit: all three at once (mario_cube:45:1:1.5)", "dark_sphere on the highest ground at (9,17)", "the threshold wall at row 20, one door at x4-6", "the motion gallery: slide at (5,21), turn at (5,22), swell at (5,23)", "all three at (3,24), the axioms card at (5,24), a plain pick_up_cube at (7,24)", "teleporter t at (5,25)" ]
